4. Finally, we could also try to reduce the number of trainable parameters by sharing weights between different parts of the network. For example, we could share the weights between the policy and value networks so that they learn similar features.

Overall, there are many ways to reduce the number of parameters in your model while still achieving good performance. It depends on what kind of trade-offs you're willing to make between accuracy and computational efficiency.

